INT. GENERATION SHIP HELIOS-9 - SEED VAULT DECK - SHIP NIGHT

A low arched chamber lined with frosted drawers of seed. Pale green grow lights hum. Condensation beads on steel.

TEODORA VASK, 50s, a quiet botanist in a faded gray jumpsuit, walks the aisle with a tablet, touching each drawer as she passes.

TEODORA
Barley, two hundred and eleven. Barley, two hundred and twelve. You're all still here. Good.

She stops at a drawer that is slightly open, closes it with a click, and makes a note.

TEODORA (CONT'D)
(to herself)
Humidity at point four. Slightly high. Always slightly high.

The hatch hisses. IMANI QUILL, 20s, in the white sash of a ship's archivist, steps in with a stack of data slates against her chest. She looks lost.

IMANI
Is this the vault? They said Deck Nine, but all the doors say Deck Nine.

TEODORA
It's the vault. You're the new archivist.

IMANI
I'm Imani. I'm sorry, I didn't know anyone would be here at this hour.

TEODORA
Nobody is, ever. That's why I come.

Imani lays her slates on a workbench and glances at the drawers.

IMANI
How many seeds are in here?

TEODORA
Eleven million, give or take. She says that, the ship, in her reports. I say it feels like more when you count them by hand.

IMANI
She doesn't mean the ship. She means the Registrar, the one who wrote the index.

TEODORA
Ah. Then she's wrong, too. She never came down here.

They share a small, tired smile. Teodora hands Imani a spare tablet.

TEODORA (CONT'D)
Start at drawer one. Read me the label on each, slowly.

IMANI
Just read?

TEODORA
Just read. I listen better than I count.

Imani sits on the stool, props the tablet on her knee, and reads aloud.

IMANI
Wheat, hard red winter. Wheat, soft white. Rye.

Teodora closes her eyes and listens.
